hypotheses.statement:
There is a homomorphism $\chi:\Gamma\to\mathbb Z$ with $$\chi(a)=1,\qquad \chi(b_i)=\chi(t)=0.$$ It satisfies $\chi(u_i)=i$ and $\chi(w)=100$. For every positive integer $M$, the action on $$Y_M=X\times\mathbb Z/M\mathbb Z,
 \qquad \nu_M=\mu\times\text{uniform measure},$$ defined by $$\label{actions:product-action}
 (x,r)g=(xg,r+\chi(g)\bmod M)$$ is free and p.m.p. on a standard Borel probability space.

Let $V_k$ be finite exact right $A$-sets, with $n_k=|V_k|\to\infty$, such that for every fixed $g\in A\setminus\{1\}$, $$\frac{|\{v\in V_k:vg=v\}|}{n_k}\longrightarrow0.
 \label{models:fixed-points}$$ For the free Bernoulli action on $X$ from Section <a href="#actions:section" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="actions:section">2</a>, whose cost agrees with the full product action on $X_0=[0,1]^\Gamma$, one has $$\delta_X\ge\limsup_{k\to\infty}
 \frac{\operatorname{rk}(D_{V_k})}{n_k}.$$

